 The [ordinary-reader map](ordinary-read-cutover.md) distinguishes content/presence and bytes-plus-real-LastWriteTimeUtc results from original physical publication receipts. It recommends common validated reads while preserving public recovery/quiescence/no-reacquire/absence behavior and explicit original entrypoints/scopes for old setup and recovery. Browser v6 before-image setup reads tracked bytes before attaching its recorder, so recorder presence or evidence-path exclusion alone is insufficient. The current B3b block does not migrate those readers; ordinary reads, later accepted publication and save/load retain their separate bounded verification.
 
 T031 implementation refinement: ordinary QTE acceptance/transport calls use the helper without callbacks; explicit AfterLegacyAcceptanceRuntimeWrittenAsync/AfterLegacyDeferredEffectMutationAsync preserve original recorder/recovery callbacks. AfterRuntimeWrittenAsync and final:* AfterDeferredEffectMutationAsync remain later domain hooks. Uncertainty bypasses domain compensation; the private Russian notice avoids unchanged-state/retry claims. This is the bounded helper/error boundary, not full accepted-turn or browser-v6 migration; current verified/unrun evidence lives in plan.md.
+
+
+## T030-F ordinary tree deletion refinement, 2026-10-01
+
+The narrow approved FR-002–007 continuation reuses `EnumerateLocalTreeFiles` and `ReadLocalFileBytesAsync` to validate the complete tree before mutation, and publishes exact file before-images to absence as one existing B1 set. `GetLocalRelativePath` preserves normalized extended Windows roots; platform comparers preserve Linux case distinctions. Absent and recursively empty trees require no zero-member journal or invented generation. Nonrecursive validated pruning is structural follow-up only. A committed result with cleanup debt must retain member parents: B1 ScratchScope grants exact sibling stage/undo paths and requires those parents during cold recovery. Cleanup/pruning/logging failure must preserve the established byte decision.
+
+Recorder presence alone cannot choose the original handler. Warm BrowserLocalWriteCoordinator clears its recorder before ExplorerLocalTurnRollbackArtifacts restores dynamic cleanup directories; pending_turn_snapshot is outside the excluded evidence root and IsLegacyStorageRecovery is false. Add an explicit original directory deletion entry at that call and preserve original evidence-parent cleanup. Cold acquisition already uses RunLegacyStorageRecoveryAsync. Do not change physical authority globally or recursively delete nonempty ordinary canonical trees without B1.
+
+The saved Linux ProcedureTerminalQuarantine failure is in preparation before its helper. Verify that exact body after the tree port, without bypassing its fixture. Complete live/console preparation remains non-atomic because request/manifest/authority/dice/snapshot operations are separate. Full preparation, browser-v6, load/save/library, worker and B4/B5 remain later work. A fresh read-only Astra XHigh investigation found no material product decision blocking this slice; focused implementation and review evidence are still pending.
+
+
+### T031 original backup prerequisite exposed after T030-F
+
+The actual Linux `ProcedureTerminalQuarantine_RemovesDurableAuthorityBeforeReleasingEveryClaim` fixture at tested `efc28137` now passes its live-preparation tree stage (Procedure.cs 1065–1079), then fails during `StateDistributor.DistributeAsync` before the fixture returns (1183–1186): `FileSystemManager.CreateBackupCore` calls the original physical `WriteFileAtomicBytesCoreAsync`, whose descriptor-bound create-only publication is unsupported on Linux. Quarantine assertions at the test's line 256 onward were not reached. Preserve this failed/unqualified Linux consumer as a later T031 backup/accepted-publication prerequisite; do not weaken or bypass its fixture, copy method, receipts, original cleanup or physical backend in T030-F. Exact console snapshot and terminal-error cleanup consumers passed in that same separate partial run.
